A k x k magic square is a k x k grid filled with integers such that every row sum, every column sum, and both diagonal sums are all equal. The integers in the magic square do not have to be distinct. Every 1 x 1 grid is trivially a magic square.
Given an m x n integer grid, return the size (i.e., the side length k) of the largest magic square that can be found within this grid.
Example 1:
Input: grid = [[7,1,4,5,6],[2,5,1,6,4],[1,5,4,3,2],[1,2,7,3,4]]
Output: 3
Explanation: The largest magic square has a size of 3.
Every row sum, column sum, and diagonal sum of this magic square is equal to 12.
- Row sums: 5+1+6 = 5+4+3 = 2+7+3 = 12
- Column sums: 5+5+2 = 1+4+7 = 6+3+3 = 12
- Diagonal sums: 5+4+3 = 6+4+2 = 12
Example 2:
Input: grid = [[5,1,3,1],[9,3,3,1],[1,3,3,8]]
Output: 2
Constraints:
m == grid.length
n == grid[i].length
1 <= m, n <= 50
1 <= grid[i][j] <= 106


package com.solutions;
public class LargestMagicSquare {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] grid1 = {
                {7, 1, 4, 5, 6},
                {2, 5, 1, 6, 4},
                {1, 5, 4, 3, 2},
                {1, 2, 7, 3, 4}
        };
        int[][] grid2 = {
                {5, 1, 3, 1},
                {9, 3, 3, 1},
                {1, 3, 3, 8}
        };

        System.out.println("Output 1: " + largestMagicSquare(grid1)); // 3
        System.out.println("Output 2: " + largestMagicSquare(grid2)); // 2
    }

    public static int largestMagicSquare(int[][] grid) {

        int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;

        // Prefix sums
        int[][] row = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        int[][] col = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        int[][] diag1 = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        int[][] diag2 = new int[m + 1][n + 2];

        // Build prefix arrays
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                row[i + 1][j + 1] = row[i + 1][j] + grid[i][j];
                col[i + 1][j + 1] = col[i][j + 1] + grid[i][j];
                diag1[i + 1][j + 1] = diag1[i][j] + grid[i][j];
                diag2[i + 1][j] = diag2[i][j + 1] + grid[i][j];
            }
        }

        int maxSize = Math.min(m, n);

        // Try from largest to smallest
        for (int size = maxSize; size >= 2; size--) {
            for (int i = 0; i + size <= m; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j + size <= n; j++) {

                    int target = row[i + 1][j + size] - row[i + 1][j];
                    boolean magic = true;

                    // Check all rows
                    for (int r = i; r < i + size; r++) {
                        if (row[r + 1][j + size] - row[r + 1][j] != target) {
                            magic = false;
                            break;
                        }
                    }

                    // Check all columns
                    for (int c = j; c < j + size && magic; c++) {
                        if (col[i + size][c + 1] - col[i][c + 1] != target) {
                            magic = false;
                            break;
                        }
                    }

                    // Check diagonals
                    int d1 = diag1[i + size][j + size] - diag1[i][j];
                    int d2 = diag2[i + size][j] - diag2[i][j + size];

                    if (magic && d1 == target && d2 == target) {
                        return size;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return 1; // 1x1 is always magic
    }
}
